# Phase 1.2 — Security Architecture Hardening: Final Report

**Date Completed:** March 2, 2026  
**Objective:** Harden authentication security from ~78% → ~88% production readiness  
**Result:** ✅ All backend + Flutter client steps implemented, compiled, deployed.

---

## Security Flow (After Phase 1.2)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App as Flutter App
    participant API as NestJS Backend
    participant DB as Supabase

    App->>App: Generate device_id (stored in SecureStorage)
    App->>API: POST /auth/request-otp {phone, device_id}
    API->>API: Check 60s cooldown + 3/10min limit
    API->>DB: Store OTP request
    API-->>App: OTP sent

    App->>API: POST /auth/verify-otp {phone, pin, device_id}
    API->>API: Check 5-attempt cap
    API->>DB: Verify device session
    Note over API,DB: If new device → increment session_version<br/>Old device tokens become invalid
    API->>DB: Delete old refresh tokens, store new hash
    API-->>App: {access_token (device_id+sv), refresh_token}

    App->>API: GET /summary/month (Bearer token)
    API->>DB: Validate token.device_id == user.active_device_id<br/>AND token.sv == user.session_version
    alt Match
        API-->>App: Dashboard data
    else Mismatch
        API-->>App: 401 SESSION_REVOKED
        App->>App: Clear tokens, redirect to login
    end
```

